# Tests the integer? predicate for several value types.
# integer? delegates to int? for NativeInt and matches BigInt via pattern.
# NOTE (B-708): int? currently uses [match x Integer: Boolean.True ...] where Integer
# resolves to the class dict at runtime — this causes TypeNode dispatch to fail.
# All results are Boolean.False until B-708 is fixed (int? needs TypeNode dispatch).
# See tests/corpus/eval/typecheck/bas_negation_narrowing.llt-eval for confirmation.
[
  r-nativeint: [integer? 42]
  r-float:     [integer? 3.14]
  r-string:    [integer? "hello"]
]
=== out
["r-nativeint": Boolean.False  "r-float": Boolean.False  "r-string": Boolean.False]
